Z||000009||fieroshop||05-22-2000||12:53 AM||||Shiner, that is not rice you smell but an 88 GT that is going thru complete transformation. We will start taking items off this week and will have a hood scoop. side scoops (original Pontiac style) and a dark green metalic paint with two coats od clear with pearlessend powder and finally three coats of clear. Then we color sand and polish and then we have to make sure that when we look into the paint we don't fall in. (The paint will look like 10 ft deep) I will post pics as soon as the GT is done. But if you have not seen my GT I posted pics of it as to what it looks like now. For those of you going to San Diego for the western regionals I'll be there with my GT.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Coconut||05-22-2000||01:09 AM||||Fieroshop, I can definately smell what your cookin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> When I decided that I wanted to paint my car green, I had envisioned the same type of wheels as well. Just out of curiosity, what color is your interior? When I get my car painted, I'm thinking of switching the interior from gray to tan to compliment that green. Boy, oh boy, I can't wait to see the finished product! Keep us posted.         Keep on Cruisin'<BR>                 Coconut||||reg||14
